      "created_at": "2017-10-10T10:23:12Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-10-10T10:23:12Z",
      "body": "The proposal is __not__  for a special kind of account but for special kinds of posts/comments for which there would be no record of the author. The accounts created by the current methods are not anonymous but __pseudonymous__.\n\nThe problems with pseudonymous accounts are,\n\n- The moment you identify the person, you can identify all his posts/comments.\n- Any hint from one post/comment can exposes the real identity.\n- Even a transaction of Steem can be traced back.\n\nThe anonymous posts/comments would not have any record of the author. And there wouldn't be any rewards connected to them. Thus the author cannot be identified.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
