      "created_at": "2017-10-10T14:00:14Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-10-10T14:00:24Z",
      "body": "If an account has a null authority (no keys, or threshold 0), then it can post without a signature. Yes, there is a name associated with it, but anyone can use it. So it is anonymous. Several users have set up accounts like this in the past. If you are asking for comments that are not even traced on the blockchain, then this is not the repository you are looking for because this is only for things on the blockchain.\r\n\r\nThe problem with no author being listed on a comment is that we have no way of rate limiting via Steem Power (no account means no Steem Power). It opens up an attack vector against the blockchain.\r\n\r\nIf there is a reason why the null authority scheme does not work, I would be interested to hear it, but I believe all of the tools to implement what you want already exist.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
